You are building the GenValue Academy website.

## Stack
- Next.js 15 (App Router), TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, Framer Motion
- Tailwind v4 uses @theme in globals.css - NO tailwind.config.ts file exists
- Brand colors are defined as CSS variables in globals.css

## Brand Colors
- Primary/Navy: #0D1B2A
- Accent Blue: #2563EB
- Emerald: #10B981
- Gold: #F59E0B
- Background: #04050A

## Rules
- Always use TypeScript. Never use `any` - use proper interfaces from src/data/course.ts
- Always use functional components with named exports
- Always add aria-labels to interactive elements
- Always handle loading and error states
- Always add dark mode variants for custom colors
- Use Framer Motion for all animations - respect prefers-reduced-motion
- Use next/image for all images with proper width, height, and alt
- Import site constants from src/lib/constants.ts
- Import course data from src/data/course.ts

## Brand
- Academy: GenValue Academy
- Instructor: Sathvik Putta
- Contact: genvalue.academy@gmail.com
- Tagline: "Choosing the Right AI Tool for Every Task"

## Security (both LMS + Admin portals)

You are an expert, security-conscious senior developer. Prioritize security over speed.

- Never hardcode API keys, secrets, or tokens in source code — use environment variables only.
- Always validate and sanitize user input on the server (email, text, URLs, uploads).
- Use Firebase Auth for student credentials; admin portal uses OTP + signed session tokens.
- Flag insecure patterns (unsigned JWT decode, missing rate limits, raw SQL with user input).
- Prefer Prisma parameterized queries; never concatenate user input into SQL strings.
- All new API routes belong under `/api/v1/`; keep `/api/` as a legacy alias only.
- Profile images: JPEG/PNG/WebP/GIF only, max 5 MB, stored on Cloudinary (never local executable paths).
- Assignment PDFs are URL-only (HTTP/HTTPS) until a dedicated upload pipeline exists.
